  <report name="WallRingDesign" title="Wall steel and annular pile rings" unit="in" pagesize="816,1056" margin="48,48,48,48" bordermargin="0,0,0,0" collapsemargins="False">
    <include target="Library.Geometry"/>
    <stylerule type="AnyEquation" name="Required Input" texthighlight="#F7E6B9"/>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">Wall steel and annular pile rings</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Fixed scalar units: inches, kip, ksi, with density in kip/ft^3 and areas per foot as labeled. Units are labels, not native dimensional quantities. This sheet recomputes the exported topology. Regenerate after changing pile/row counts, bar size/coating, automatic spacing, or contact assumptions. Two continuous top/bottom fillets. Values are not design acceptance. Case 5778a133d8f0.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">SHARING: Midplane tributaries assign vertical force and the ring rows share the pile-head moment equally; all rings are assumed to engage. Concrete transfer (including concrete below rings), splitting/breakout and row compatibility need a separately substantiated load path.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">STIFFNESS: Ring moments follow pile-head rotational stiffness against the rigid-wall rotation (D-070). The free length to fixity and the axial spring length are entered values (defaults from the pier pile case with sand depth to fixity, LRFD 10.7.3.13.4; tip elevation pending). Lateral, thermal, unsymmetric and construction-stage rotations enter only through the imposed rotation input.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">SCOPE: Wall checks cover minimum shrinkage/temperature steel and detailing only. Wall flexure, shear, lateral loads, seismic and strength load paths are outside this calculation.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">CONNECTION: Local plate and double-fillet checks do not establish pipe-shell bending/ovalization, global pile interaction, ring-segment splices, fatigue, corrosion or WPS/fabrication adequacy.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">BASIS: Confirm geometry, exposure/cover, material grades, construction joints and bar anchorage routing. Starting dimensions are the earlier study snapshot, not a current CAD import.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
